                <pb facs="0116" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg32"/>

                <head>No. 21.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Tree.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 18,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch No. 89, of the 6th instant,
                    in which you state that the Commission appointed on the condition of industrial
                    labor in Belgium has organized and commenced its sessions, has been received. I
                    shall be much obliged to you for reports as to the proceedings of the
                    Commission, and as to the conclusion reached by it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
